{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the son of the Israelite woman went out, and blasphemed.</b> In the course of the quarrel he blasphemed." "<b>And he went out and blasphemed.</b> It does not say ויברך, as in the matter said of Navot: ״ברך נבות אלקים ומלך,״ but rather <b>ויקלל</b> — this teaches that one is not executed for a kinui (a substitute name)." "<b>Et HaShem, and he blasphemed.</b> Rabbi Yosi the Egyptian said: they were defilers and defiled Israel. The Sages said: she was the wife of Neria, grandson of Dan — her name was Shelomit bat Dibri. That night, Pharaoh's taskmasters came upon him and killed him, and came upon his wife and she conceived. And everything follows the seed: if sweet, sweet; if bitter, bitter. And when Israel went out of Egypt, they strove in the camp — the son of the Israelite woman and the Israelite man. His fellow said to him: you are a mamzer, the son of an Egyptian man. The son of the Israelite woman asked: where is my father? They said to him: he is the one whom Moshe killed by the explicit name. That mamzer, who was the son of the Israelite woman, began to curse and blaspheme that name — that is what is written: ״ויקב את השם״ — that explicit name by which his father was killed." "<b>Of the tribe of Dan.</b> He caused the quarrel, for that one who would say 'judge my case' — they said to him: you come from Dan, as it is written: ״דן ידין עמו״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:57.810721542Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}